course: dictionary
lesson: 1205
title: Capital letters and meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter can change what a word means. «The Buddha was a teacher who lived in ancient India.» Here Buddha, with a big B, is a name. It means one special teacher who started Buddhism.
explain: Now look at «a buddha» with a small b. A buddha can be a statue of him, or a person who has become fully awake. The sentence «"Buddha" means "awakened one"» tells you the word's core meaning: awake and aware.
explain: To check which meaning fits, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence is about a teacher who lived long ago, the name is right. If it is about a statue in a garden, a buddha is the statue.
fact: The Buddha was a teacher who lived in ancient India and started Buddhism.
fact: A buddha is a statue or picture of the Buddha, or a person who has become fully awake or enlightened.
fact: «Buddha» means «the awakened one».
fact: Buddhists generally see the Buddha as a teacher, not as a god.
fact: Buddhism was founded in India about 2500 years ago by Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha.
exercise: «Buddhism was founded by Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha, in India about 2500 years ago.» Who is the Buddha in this sentence? | A statue in a temple garden | A type of food | A king who ruled the sea | *A teacher who started Buddhism
exercise: «The garden had a buddha made of stone, sitting under a tree.» What is a buddha in this sentence? | A teacher from ancient India | A kind of tree | *A statue | A type of music
exercise: «"Buddha" means "awakened one".» What does awakened mean? | *Fully awake and aware | Still fast asleep | Lost in the dark | Very loud and noisy
test: Which word is the name of one special teacher? | *Buddha, with a capital B | Both mean only a statue | buddha, with a small b | Neither word is a name
test: Buddhists say the Buddha taught kindness and calm. What did he teach? | How to fly | How to cook rice | *Kindness, calm and the end of suffering | How to build temples
exam: «The buddha in the temple was very old.» What does buddha mean in this sentence? | A kind of temple roof | A teacher's name | *A statue | A person who is always cold
